<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product & Offer Portfolio Planning -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product & Offer Portfolio Planning">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Develop strategies for products at the portfolio level.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.2.1.2</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Product & Offer Portfolio Planning Product & Offer Portfolio Planning processes develop strategies for products at the portfolio level. The decision is made as to which product types the enterprise wants or needs to offer, and how it plans to enter or grow in these sectors. This will be done based on multiple inputs: including Enterprise Strategies, Market Research and Market Analysis.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Gather & Analyze Product Information -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Gather & Analyze Product Information">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Research information relating to product ideas and opportunities and identify product opportunities.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.2.1.2.1</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.1.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Gather & Analyze Product Information Gather & Analyze Product Information processes research information relating to product ideas and opportunities and identify product opportunities based on the analysis of external and internal information sources. These processes encompass analysis to identify new products as well as reviewing existing products. They also include the establishment and management of relationships with external providers of product information, and the management of internal resources used for providing product information.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Gather Product Information -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Gather Product Information">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Establish and management of external providers and internal  resources for providing product information.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.2.1.2.1.1</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.1.1.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Gather Product Information Gather Product information processes  focus on establishment  and Management of relationships with external providers of product information, and management of internal resources used for providing product information.

Information may also be gathered by interacting with processes that perform competitive analysis, market research, and market analysis.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Analyze Product Information -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Analyze Product Information">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Identify new product offerings, review existing product offerings, research information about product offering ideas.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.2.1.2.1.2</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.1.1.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Analyze Product Information Analyze Product information processes focus on research of information relating to product ideas and opportunities and identify product opportunities based on analysis of the external and internal information sources. These processes are responsible for analysis to identify new product offerings as well as review of existing product offerings.

If new resource and/or service infrastructure is needed then this process interacts with the processes that develop resource strategies and/or service strategies to insure new product offerings can be developed. Similarly interaction with market/sales strategy processes may result if new sales channels or market segments are needed.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Establish Product Portfolio Strategy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Establish Product Portfolio Strategy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Define and agree the product and offer portfolio structure to be used within the enterprise.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.2.1.2.2</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.1.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Establish Product Portfolio Strategy The Establish Product Portfolio Strategy processes define the overall structure of the product portfolios to be used across the enterprise, or between or within business units. These products and product portfolios form the basis of offers made to customers. It includes the agreement on and implementation of cross-portfolio and cross-product co-ordination and management functions.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Overall Product Portfolios Structure -->

