<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Specification Test Development & Retirement -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Specification Test Development & Retirement">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Product Test Development & Retirement is in charge of the Product Test catalog.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Product Specification Test Development & Retirement Product Test Development &amp; Retirement is in charge of the Product Test catalog.
A type of Product Test aims at measuring proper functioning and capacities of a Product whatever the context is (Product Specification Development &amp; Retirement, Order Handling, Customer Order Orchestration, Product Performance Management, Customer Problem Handling, Product Test Management).
Product Test Development &amp; Retirement includes:
- Specifying in detail each Product Test according to the different context. It includes specifying:

	the roles authorized to use the Test and quotas for each type of role
	 the method to conduct the Test
	 the rules that define the strategies for conducting the test (including  the test plan)
	 the thresholds and related actions
	 the relationships with lower level tests (Service Test or Resource Test)
	the report of test results with rules for enrichment of Service &amp; Resource Tests results according to role asking for it

- Specifying test scenarios defining sequence of Tests with rules about context and planning to trigger it. It includes roles allowed for asking test scenario and corresponding quotas.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Capacity Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Capacity Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Capability Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Product Capacity Management business process manages the activities required to ensure a business is able to plan, model, analyze, optimize, monitor and report product capacity, and related constraints according the commercial objectives in a timely and e</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.8</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Product Capacity Management Product Capacity Management business process manages the activities required to ensure a business is able to plan, model, analyze, optimize, monitor and report product capacity, and related constraints according the commercial objectives in a timely and effective manner.
The underlying business activities supporting Product Capacity Management ensure that there is an effective understanding and management of Products Capacity in line with commercial demand and objectives, along with all the underlying production constraints.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Plan Product Capacity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Plan Product Capacity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Capability Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Plan Product Capacity business activity determine the design and organization of the production capacity management activities needed to meet changing demands for products over a period of time, as well as implement the plan for product capacity needs.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.8.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Plan Product Capacity Plan Product Capacity business activity determine the design and organization of the production capacity management activities needed to meet changing demands for products over a period of time, as well as implement the plan for product capacity needs.
A Product's capacity plan ensures Product Management: 

	aligns capacity planning strategies with both commercial and operational goals,


	ensures that there are sufficient product capacity to support planned and forecasted commercial objectives,
	identifies gaps in capacity allocation early,
	determines product capacity needs according to demand,
	determines constraints and usage patterns over time,
	forecasts future capacity needs,
	and communicates products capacity requirements in time.

In the context of capacity planning, consideration is given to all input requirements, conversion processes and outputs when planning product capacity.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

