<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Analyze Product Capacity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Capability Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Analyze Product Capacity business activity establishes and models insights, patterns and changes to product capacity, by assessing potential capacity and the actual capacity a product currently achieves.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.8.8</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Analyze Product Capacity Analyze Product Capacity business activity establishes and models insights, patterns and changes to product capacity, by assessing potential capacity and the actual capacity a product currently achieves.

This business activity covers collection of product-related data (usage data, performance data, operational data etc.) to support Product Managers to identify patterns and insights relating to a product.

Analyze Product Capacity support Product Capacity Management by providing relevant and timely insights, including available inventory holding capacity, products "time and material" capacity, etc. and how capacity utilization (allocated, in-use, unused) can be optimized to increase business value.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

