<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Add data to the records from sources such as customer, product, or other reference data to augment the product usage records.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.1.1.14.1.1</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.16.1.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Add Product Usage Data Not used for this process element.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Assign Product Usage Price -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Assign Product Usage Price">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Billing"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Assign a price to product usage without consideration of specific product or customer information. The assigned price may be used to enrich the product usage record.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.1.1.14.1.2</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.16.1.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Assign Product Usage Price Not used for this process element</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Guide and Assign Product Usages -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Guide and Assign Product Usages">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Billing"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Ensures that the product usage records used in the billing processes are related to the correct customer billing account and subscribed products.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.1.1.14.2</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.16.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Guide and Assign Product Usages The Guide Product Usages processes ensure that the event records used in the billing process relate to the correct customer billing account and products.  A specific product usage record may be related to multiple customer billing accounts and subscribed products. 
  
Distribution of product usage records to other processes may also occur.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

