<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.1.1.22.1.1</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.1.1.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Ensure Customer Interface Capability element Ensure that there is capability (for example, information, materials, systems and resource) so that the Customer Interface Management processes can operate effectively when a contact with a customer occurs. Examples are information on how to handle unusual requests based on temporary situations, systems needed to accept and track customer contacts, requests for the provisioning of additional resources where it has been identified that current levels will impact on timely contact handling. These processes are responsible for implementing generic and specific changes to customer interfaces. This support includes localization support and personalization support, and it could be in updating agent scripts, IVR announcements, Web pages, etc. Customer Interface Support processes keep up to date all information concerning customers.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

