<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.21.5</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Identify Issues and Provide Reports - Identifying any technical driven shortcomings of the party inventory repository, and providing input to Resource Development & Management processes to rectify these issues.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business Partner Privacy Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business Partner Privacy Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Business Partner Privacy Management processes manage the privacy requirements of business partners in accordance with information privacy requirements, and regulatory mandates.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Business Partner Privacy Management Business Partner Privacy Management processes manage the privacy requirements of business partners in accordance with information privacy requirements, and regulatory mandates.
These processes help to:
Define the Business Partner Privacy Management scope
Define the information that constitutes Personally Identifiable Information (personal identifiable information) where Privacy Policy applies.
Define Default Privacy requirements for each type of personal identifiable information
Capture explicit consent and define with Privacy Policy according to wishes of the organization
Modify/update Privacy Policy according to future needs or requirements
Enforce the Business Partner Privacy Policy and ensure that information is managed correctly according to stated privacy policies.
Communicate relevant personal identifiable information processing standards to third parties with whom the information is shared</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Business Partner Privacy Definition -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Business Partner Privacy Definition">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage Business Partner Privacy Definition process manage the definition of the privacy management that applies to a particular category of business partner (data processor, data controller, or other third party etc.).</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Business Partner Privacy Definition Manage Business Partner Privacy Definition process manage the definition of the privacy management that applies to a particular category of business partner (data processor, data controller, or other third party etc.).
It is used to determine the legal expectations of partners that want to apply and use personally identifiable information in or across jurisdiction, location, regulation, and standards).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile Agreement and Amendment -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile Agreement and Amendment">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile Agreement and Amendment processes provides data subjects the ability to create agreement with a data processing business partner about processing of their information.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile Agreement and Amendment Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile Agreement and Amendment processes provides data subjects the ability to create agreement with a data processing business partner about processing of their information.
This process is used to prove the conformance with Laws & Regulation, particularly showing the explicit consent and information about the Purposes and Retention of any personal identifiable information.
It creates the agreement regarding the privacy management of a data subject. In all engagement with data subject, an agreement with the privacy policy needs to be acknowledged.
Depending on the flexibility of the personal identifiable information privacy attributes, the data subject can agree to some requirement or change them.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile process is used to manage the Privacy Profile for each Business Partner Type, including the enforcement of the Business Partner Privacy Profile.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile Manage Business Partner Privacy Profile process is used to handle the life cycle of the business partners privacy profile.
This process is crucial to business partner privacy management, because it helps the partnering entities processing data to conform with Laws & Regulation and 'privacy by design' principles.
It is composed of:
Enforcement of the Business Partner Privacy Profile, meaning the application of the Privacy Rules for each purpose/retention, both internal and external, of all personal identifiable information.
Import/export of the Privacy Profile for each element of personal identifiable information received or sent from or to another partner or party involved in the processing of personal identifiable information.
Modify a Privacy Profile, through dashboards or consent
Meet other requirements from regional Laws & Regulations, such as the demonstration of compliance, the 'right of erasure' or 'right to be forgotten'.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Business Partner Privacy Location and Regulation -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Business Partner Privacy Location and Regulation">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Define Business Partner Privacy Location and Regulation process establish how the relevant privacy regulations that must be followed are to be identified.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.3.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Define Business Partner Privacy Location and Regulation Define Business Partner Privacy Location and Regulation process is used to:
Identify the locations (regulatory jurisdiction) related to a business partner relationship and/or engagement.
Define the locations where business partners can process information
Define the privacy regulations that apply to locations
Define the dominant regulation
Define the highest standards that apply for multiple legislative locations</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Enforce Business Partner Privacy Profile -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Enforce Business Partner Privacy Profile">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Enforce Business Partner Privacy Profile process manages the application of the Business Partner privacy profile so that any third party processing such data can comply with mandatory legislation, and the agreed wish of the business partner.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.3.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Enforce Business Partner Privacy Profile Enforce Business Partner Privacy Profile process manages the application of the Business Partner privacy profile so that any third party processing such data can comply with mandatory legislation, and the agreed wish of the business partner.
For each action performed by the third party processing personal identifiable information data of the business partner, the third party processing such data must ensure their action is compliant with the rules set by default, and validated or amended by the business partner.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Erase Data Subject Privacy Profile Information -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Erase Data Subject Privacy Profile Information">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>"Erase Data Subject Privacy Profile Information process ensures that all data subject information referenced in the Privacy Profile according to business partner data processing rules are erased.
"</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.3.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Erase Data Subject Privacy Profile Information Erase Data Subject Privacy Profile Information process ensures that all data subject information referenced in the Privacy Profile according to business partner data processing rules are erased.
It can be done according to data subjects' request, or retention rules.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Import Data Subject Privacy Profile -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Import Data Subject Privacy Profile">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Import Data Subject Privacy Profile process ingests the privacy profile pre-defined by a data subject, and integrates it into the privacy profile.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.3.4</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Import Data Subject Privacy Profile Import Data Subject Privacy Profile process ingests the privacy profile pre-defined by a data subject, and integrates it into the privacy profile.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Modify Business Partner Privacy Policy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Modify Business Partner Privacy Policy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Modify Business Partner Privacy Profile process is used to modify the rules of privacy profiles following an agreement of a privacy profile between a business partner and a data subject.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.3.5</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Modify Business Partner Privacy Policy Modify Business Partner Privacy Profile process is used to modify the rules of privacy profiles following an agreement of a privacy profile between a business partner and a data subject. 
Such modifications may occur in the Dashboard and honored according to the requirements stipulated by a by privacy policy type.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Receive Customer Privacy Profile -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Receive Customer Privacy Profile">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Receive Privacy Profile process is used to receive a Profile from a data processing entity.
This process ensures that all the authorization required are agreed by the data subject, else a request for changing it will be triggered.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.3.6</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Receive Customer Privacy Profile Receive Privacy Profile process is used to receive a Profile from a data processing entity.
This process ensures that all the authorization required are agreed by the data subject, else a request for changing it will be triggered.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Request Privacy Profile Extension -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Request Privacy Profile Extension">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Request Privacy Profile Extension process is used by a data processing entity to request the change of privacy profile rule after agreement has been reached between a data processing entity and a data subject.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.3.7</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Request Privacy Profile Extension Request Privacy Profile Extension process is used by a data processing entity to request the change of privacy profile rule after agreement has been reached between a data processing entity and a data subject.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Send Privacy Profile -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Send Privacy Profile">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness & Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Send Privacy Profile process communicates a Privacy Policy Profile attached to a personal identifiable information to a data processing entity .</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.22.3.8</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Send Privacy Profile Send Privacy Profile process manages the application of external privacy policy rules, when personal identifiable information must be sent to a data processing entity. 
It applies the external rules, then transforms the existing customer privacy profile external rules into internal rules, in order the Data Processor Party can import it into its Privacy Management.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Strategic & Enterprise Planning Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Strategic & Enterprise Planning Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Strategic & Enterprise Planning Management business process directs and controls the developmenet of strategy and plans of the organization as a whole.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.3.1</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Strategic & Enterprise Planning Management Strategic &amp; Enterprise Planning Management business process directs and controls the developmenet of strategy and plans of the organization as a whole. 

Strategic &amp; Enteprise Planning Management includes business activities that develop Strategic plans of the organization's focus, including which markets the enterprise will address, what financial requirements must be met, what acquisitions may enhance the enterprise's financial or market position, etc., and enterprise planning to coordinate the overall plan for the organization in teandem with operating business units. 
This is the business processes that drives the mission and vision of the organization as a whole, with oversight on the enterprise architecture management, corporate investment strategies, and organizational capacity management.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Plan Strategic Business -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Plan Strategic Business">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Plan Strategic Business activity define and develop the orgnization's direction - the Corporate stratgy, including the vision and direction.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.3.1.1</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.1.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Plan Strategic Business Plan Strategic Business activity define and develop the orgnization's direction - the Corporate stratgy, including the vision and direction.

Plan Strategic Business activity understands the organization and its core business, continuosly analyzes strengths, weaknesses and threats, defines the vision, objectives and goals of the organization as a whole, and effectively institutionalizes corporate strategic plans into action (which includes monitoring underlying business plans for alignment and contirbution to the success of the organization).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Provide Strategic Business Direction -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Provide Strategic Business Direction">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Provide strategic business direction to the enterprise</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.3.1.1.1</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.1.1.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
