<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage Supply Chain Policies business activity manage the definition of principles of action that are adopted or proposed by the for all supply chain activities, including procurement and logistics, warehousing, transport and physical resource distributio</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.10.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Supply Chain Policies Manage Supply Chain Policies business activity manage the definition of principles of action that are adopted or proposed by the for all supply chain activities, including procurement and logistics, warehousing, transport and physical resource distribution, and supervise their application.
Plans will capture warehousing policies, inventory/stock policies, logistics policies, production policies and fulfillment policies.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

