<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Enterprise Performance Policy & Procedure -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Enterprise Performance Policy & Procedure">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage Performance Policy & Procedure business activity is in charge of directing and controlling performance fairness (equity and/equitability) and procedure consistency across all areas defined for enterprise performance management.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.13.4.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Enterprise Performance Policy & Procedure Manage Performance Policy & Procedure business activity is in charge of directing and controlling performance fairness (equity and/equitability) and procedure consistency across all areas defined for enterprise performance management.
This business activity provide management with tasks and guides that enable clear communication on the standards of activities, tasks and performance expectation to ensure performance standards are met.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Business Process Performance -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Business Process Performance">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage Business Process Performance business activity is in charge of directing controlling how efficient or effective business processes in the enterprise are defined and operationalized.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.13.4.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Business Process Performance Manage Business Process Performance business activity is in charge of directing controlling how efficient or effective business processes in the enterprise are defined and operationalized.

Manage Business Process Performance business activity supports checking the achievement of strategic and operational goals, as well as decision-making for the continuous optimization of business processes.

This business activity will also define the methodology to be employed in process design, process change management or process re-engineering activities across the enterprise. Cost and performance of individual business process activities is the accountability of core areas using the business process. This business activity will as part of controlling, monitor the value of the overall process management activities to ensure that the enterprise continues to achieve performance objects established. Appropriate reports on business process performance at the enterprise level are produced in line with Manage Performance Reporting business activities.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Enterprise Performance Data -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Enterprise Performance Data">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage Enterprise Performance Data business activity is in charge of collecting and analyzing enterprise performance data.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.3.3.4.2</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.13.4.4</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Enterprise Performance Data Manage Enterprise Performance Data business activity is in charge of collecting and analyzing enterprise performance data.
Note that performance is actually assessed within each area of the enterprise, but follows the guidelines defined by this process, which provides a template for specific applications of Performance Assessment in any areas of the Enterprise.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Verify Performance Data -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Verify Performance Data">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Verify Performance Data business activity handles all tasks that make sure or demonstrate that enterprise performance data are true, accurate or justified.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.13.4.4.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Verify Performance Data Verify Performance Data business activity handles all tasks that make sure or demonstrate that enterprise performance data are true, accurate or justified. 
The tasks here include verifying consistency of independent records of information related to all core processes altogether i.e. market, customer, product, service, business partner and resources within. It works with Manage Performance Consolidation, Reconciliation and Close and undertakes synchronization performance data across all core and enterprise activities for consistency.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Enterprise Performance Reporting -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Enterprise Performance Reporting">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage Performance Reporting business activity provide the planning and reporting needed to achieve business outcomes. Manage Performance Reporting helps to promote a continuous improvement feedback loop where reports on activities and performance provi</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.13.5</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Enterprise Performance Reporting Manage Performance Reporting business activity provide the planning and reporting needed to achieve business outcomes.

Performance reporting involves planning (including the production of the priorities and strategies overview and the supplemental information) for any legislative review. It includes reporting on the plans, including annual reports.

Performance reporting is designed to help:
- clarify organizational goals and directions;
- communicate the priorities of the organization;
- monitor progress and make continuous improvement;
- support budgeting and resource allocation decisions; and
- provide information to legislators, the public, media and others about the work of the organization.

Manage Performance Reporting helps to promote a continuous improvement feedback loop where reports on activities and performance provide important information to allow for the best possible decision-making in the next planning cycle.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

